# Redirect and rewrite rules, in Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` syntax:
#
#   <request path>   <target>   <status>
#
# The status code decides the behavior. 3xx sends the browser elsewhere; 4xx
# serves a custom error page with that status; 200 rewrites (serves another
# asset's body at this URL without changing it). All of them are certified.

/old              /new.html              301   # permanent redirect, internal
/legacy           https://example.com/   302   # temporary redirect, external
/missing-page     /404.html              404   # custom Not Found page
/gone-page        /410.html              410   # custom Gone page
/about            /about.html            200   # rewrite: pretty URL for a file
/blog/*           /blog/index.html       200   # rewrite: whole subtree to one page
